    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0194" n="78" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg78"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/1304.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The present coalition Government is nominally in possession of 20 Provinces,
                    under military governors the extent of whose submission to the central
                    Government is problematical. The north and south are not yet well fused, but the
                    only organized resistance is in Mongolia, <pb facs="0195" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/>
                    Kanush, Turkestan and Thibet. There is acquiescence but not hearty support on
                    the part of the wealthy and educated, and the real will of the mass of the
                    people is not known. The National Council cannot therefore be considered
                    representative. The Government was established by the political manoeuvers of a
                    few, not by general demand of the people. But it is the only government in
                    sight, and recognition would strengthen its hold on the country, particularly if
                    given by concerted action of the powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
